is, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of process evaluation within Public Policy and Governance, particularly where the Policy Evaluation module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of process evaluation, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Assessment of how a policy or programme was implemented, including whether activities reached intended participants and followed the planned delivery process. Within Policy Evaluation, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of process evaluation within Public Policy and Governance, particularly where the Policy Evaluation module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of process evaluation, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'process evaluation; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of process evaluation, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Public Policy and Governance', 'Active'), ('KCR_001213', 'outcome evaluation', 'Social Science', 'Public Policy and Governance', 'Policy / Governance Concept', 'Assessment of whether a policy or programme produced its intended outcomes and the extent to which observed changes can reasonably be attributed to the intervention.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of outcome evaluation within Public Policy and Governance, particularly where the Policy Evaluation module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of outcome evaluation, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable a